"""Fail-closed policy for a test run that executed nothing.

Importable on purpose, for the same reason `daemon_backlog.spl` is:
`test_runner_client.spl` is a standalone script with a bare `fn main` and
cannot be imported by a spec (documented fn-main collision), so the DECISION
lives here where a unit spec can pin it and the client keeps only the I/O.

WHY THIS POLICY EXISTS — measured 2026-08-21.

Two concurrent `simple test <spec>` processes in the same worktree could make
one of them return rc=0 with ZERO test output: no examples, no failure, no
verdict line. 42 of 122 spec logs in a 2-way sharded run came back that way,
and a serial re-run of the same specs was clean. Every sweep that reads exit
codes scored those 42 as PASSED.

The mechanism was in the shared light-daemon lane (duplicate daemons racing to
answer the same request — see light_daemon.spl `claim_lane`), but the reason it
was INVISIBLE is here: the client returned the child's exit code verbatim, so
an empty response body carried a 0 straight out to the caller.

Every real spec execution ends with a `SPEC FILE VERDICT:` line — emitted by
test_runner_single.spl, and synthesised by the daemon and by the client for a
killed worker. So "exited 0 and produced no verdict line" is exactly "ran zero
examples", and a runner given >= 1 spec that executed nothing must never exit
0, no matter which lane lost the output.

# @req REQ-TESTRUNNER-NO-EXAMPLES-FAIL-CLOSED
"""

val NO_EXAMPLES_VERDICT_MARKER: text = "SPEC FILE VERDICT:"

fn output_has_verdict(output: text) -> bool:
    """True when a run's captured output carries at least one verdict line."""
    output.contains(NO_EXAMPLES_VERDICT_MARKER)

fn no_examples_exit_code(output: text, code: i64) -> i64:
    """Exit code a spec run must report, given its output and the child's code.

    A non-zero child code is passed through untouched — it is already loud.
    A zero code with no verdict line is rewritten to 1: that is the silent
    false green this module exists to close. A zero code WITH a verdict line
    is a genuine pass and stays 0."""
    if code != 0:
        return code
    if output_has_verdict(output):
        return 0
    1

fn no_examples_is_silent_green(output: text, code: i64) -> bool:
    """True when this result is a run that executed nothing yet claimed success."""
    code == 0 and not output_has_verdict(output)
